        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-188721101:L80",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 320
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L81",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 81,
      "text": "4. Respondent in support of his case examined himself as RW-1 and his brother Sh. Bhagwan Dass, the alleged sub-lessee, as RW-2. Both the witnesses deposed that Sh. Bhagwan Dass was working as an employee and drawing a salary of Rs. 10,000/- per month. The fact of Sh. Bhagwan Dass operating the shop and being in possession of key thereof was admitted. No proof of any other employee was produced. Salary vouchers of payment of salary to Sh. Bhagwan Dass were also not proved.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "9f24acff31fcdb4e628f40dc375c31b2f4910478a5d98db6f0709b972515c208",
          "raw_char_range": [
            5046,
            5523
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            5180,
            5657
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 79,
          "original_line": 81
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-188721101:L81",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 477
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L82",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 82,
      "text": "Payment register of the salary was also not proved.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "9f24acff31fcdb4e628f40dc375c31b2f4910478a5d98db6f0709b972515c208",
          "raw_char_range": [
            5529,
            5580
          ],
