        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-188721101:L82",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L83",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 83,
      "text": "5. Trial Court by the impugned judgment took the view that the fact of sub tenancy was not established. Trial court held that it was only a privilege or a licence by the tenant in favour of his brother to use the premises, which licence or privilege could be terminated at the sweet will and pleasure of respondent. Therefore, the arrangement did not amount to assignment or parting with the possession.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "9f24acff31fcdb4e628f40dc375c31b2f4910478a5d98db6f0709b972515c208",
          "raw_char_range": [
            5586,
            5989
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            5720,
            6123
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 81,
          "original_line": 83
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-188721101:L83",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 403
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L84",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 84,
      "text": "Further, it was the trial court's view that Bhagwan Dass was not a stranger or outsider but a family member of the respondent, therefore, sub-letting cannot be inferred.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "9f24acff31fcdb4e628f40dc375c31b2f4910478a5d98db6f0709b972515c208",
          "raw_char_range": [
            5995,
            6164
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            6129,
            6298
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 82,
          "original_line": 84
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-188721101:L84",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 169
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L85",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 85,
      "text": "6.1 Aggrieved by the impugned judgment, present appeal has been preferred. Sh. R.K. Jain, counsel for appellant has argued RCT no. 52/2019 Smt. Promila Jain Vs. Ramesh Kumar Page 3 of 10 pages Digitally signed by NAROTTAM NAROTTAM KAUSHAL KAUSHAL Date:",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "9f24acff31fcdb4e628f40dc375c31b2f4910478a5d98db6f0709b972515c208",
          "raw_char_range": [
            6170,
            6422
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
