    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L86",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 86,
      "text": "> 2023.09.11 12:58:26 +0530 that trial court committed a grave error in not appreciating the fact that respondent - tenant had for all intents and purposes given possession of demised premises to his brother. Respondent was running the same business from another premises in the vicinity. He had not been visiting the premises in question at all. Respondent's brother Sh.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "9f24acff31fcdb4e628f40dc375c31b2f4910478a5d98db6f0709b972515c208",
          "raw_char_range": [
            6428,
            6799
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            6562,
            6933
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 84,
          "original_line": 86
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-188721101:L86",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 371
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L87",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 87,
      "text": "Bhagwan Dass, who was also a tenant of the petitioner in another premises, was not operating therefrom and rather operating from the demised premises, which indicates that Sh. Bhagwan Dass had shifted his business to the demised premises. The story of respondent's brother Sh. Bhagwan Dass being an employee as put forth by the respondent and his brother was not established. Therefore, the possession of respondent's brother Sh. Bhagwan Dass is deemed to be in his independent capacity.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "9f24acff31fcdb4e628f40dc375c31b2f4910478a5d98db6f0709b972515c208",
          "raw_char_range": [
            6805,
            7292
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            6939,
            7426
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 85,
          "original_line": 87
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-188721101:L87",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 487
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-188721101:L88",
      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 88,
      "text": "Another story, which has come forth in the testimony of RW-2, that tenant Sh. Ramesh Kumar had undergone angioplasty and was, therefore, not in a position to run the shop was neither pleaded nor proved by medical evidence. It is next argued that the matter is being pursued by respondent's brother Sh. Bhagwan Dass, who has been appearing before the Court even in the appeal.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-188721101-0.txt",
