      "source_document": "188721101",
      "original_line": 89,
      "text": "> 6.2 Respondent's counsel chose not to address oral arguments despite opportunity. Written submissions filed by the respondent on record have been gone through; wherein, it is submitted that there is no error in the judgment rendered by the learned ARC. Respondent having parted with possession and not being in possession of the premises has been disputed and denied. It is submitted that Sh. Bhagwan Dass was working with the respondent as an employee for the last 20 years on monthly remuneration.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "188721101",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188721101/",
